  "notes": [
    "73 VM image-conversion, restore-repair, persistence-admission and checkpoint-state methods move to interp/persist.rs. Public API signatures and DTO paths remain unchanged. The existing persistence.rs generated traversal implementation is unchanged; the moved methods call it rather than rebuilding field inventories.",
    "Seven VM source-lock targets and the snapshot side-table source-lock suite passed before the move. Normal and mutation readers for runtime-key admission, persisted-native holders and snapshot quiescence now read the actual method module. GC and allocation source inventories also include it. All moved methods were outside the historical call_native..concat_add capacity interval; its explicit moved-module coverage is unchanged.",
    "The 48 common snapshot benchmark controls completed before runtime edits and again after all validation processes finished. No concurrent builds/tests started by this task overlap timing. The unchanged run.py compare and validate_reference enforce the 1.25x gate, and all reports are retained.",
    "This incremental F142 comparison does not establish full 1A performance acceptance against the original decomposition baseline.",
    "A separate fixed three-trial audit uses before/after, after/before, before/after order against archived 3f74f5c34; all six reports are retained. Median-of-trial results do not erase initial failures or establish their cause.",
    "Independent adversarial review verified all 73 methods, leading comments and attributes, scoped helper visibility, unchanged public signatures/DTO locations, live-linking exclusions, and complete source-lock carry. The empty trailing impl block was removed after its checkpoint methods moved.",
    "Full engine CI passed 1490 tests with 26 ignored over 185 targets; SQLite passed 116 with 3 ignored. All seven validation commands exited 0. VM rustdoc reported 61 existing warnings."
  ],
